      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When semi-metallic pads exceed their optimal operating temperature, the organic binders and matrix materials can begin to degrade or decompose. This thermal breakdown alters the pad's composition, leading to the formation of a layer of gas or volatile compounds rather than a stable friction layer. This instability results in inconsistent friction, often manifesting as brake fade or erratic grabbing as the chemical balance of the pad changes under intense thermal stress. Essentially, the materials are changing their fundamental properties under extreme heat.",
      "source": "target",
